    <item>
      <title>Project information</title>
      <link>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/development/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/development/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h1 id=&#34;project-information&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Project information&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/development/#project-information&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Project information&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Project information&#34; href=&#34;#project-information&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This project is written in &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://www.swift.org&#34;&#xA;&gt;Swift&lt;/a&gt;. Started in Swift version 5.7&#xA;and moved on to Swift 5.9. It&amp;rsquo;s done with grate support from the &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://vapor.codes&#34;&#xA;&gt;Vapor&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;framework and the &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://www.swift.org/server/&#34;&#xA;&gt;Swift Server Workgroup&lt;/a&gt; community.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please check out the &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://www.serversideswift.info&#34;&#xA;&gt;server side swift&lt;/a&gt; conference if you are interested.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Uitsmijter chooses swift, because of:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;safety&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Strongly Typed&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;encourages to write clean and consistent code&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;safeguards&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Well-designed asynchronous programming interface&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;performance&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Small footprint&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Quick startup time&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Deterministic performance&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;software design patterns&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;code-structure&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Code structure&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/development/#code-structure&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Code structure&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Code structure&#34; href=&#34;#code-structure&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://www.swift.org&#34;&#xA;&gt;Swift&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s history and also &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://vapor.codes&#34;&#xA;&gt;Vapor&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s boilerplate&amp;rsquo;s sort code into&#xA;folders according to their &lt;strong&gt;technical role&lt;/strong&gt;. For example: all controllers, like login-routes, metrics-routes, etc. are&#xA;stored in the &lt;code&gt;Controllers&lt;/code&gt; folder. All models are stored in &lt;code&gt;Models&lt;/code&gt; etc. Often, you see projects with all&#xA;extensions in a &lt;code&gt;Extensions&lt;/code&gt; folder, etc&amp;hellip;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Toolchain</title>
      <link>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/tooling/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/tooling/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h1 id=&#34;commandline-tool-to-build-uitsmijter---toolingsh&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Commandline Tool To Build Uitsmijter - Tooling.sh&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/tooling/#commandline-tool-to-build-uitsmijter---toolingsh&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Commandline Tool To Build Uitsmijter - Tooling.sh&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Commandline Tool To Build Uitsmijter - Tooling.sh&#34; href=&#34;#commandline-tool-to-build-uitsmijter---toolingsh&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A build tool is a set of tools that automate the process of testing, compiling, assembling, and packaging source&#xA;code into executable software. Build tools are an essential part of the software development lifecycle, helping&#xA;developers manage the complexity of building, testing, and deploying software.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Test Cluster Domains</title>
      <link>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/test_cluster/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/test_cluster/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h1 id=&#34;test-cluster-domains&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Test Cluster Domains&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/test_cluster/#test-cluster-domains&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Test Cluster Domains&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Test Cluster Domains&#34; href=&#34;#test-cluster-domains&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When running &lt;code&gt;run-cluster&lt;/code&gt; from the &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/tooling&#34;&#xA;&gt;Toolchain&lt;/a&gt; command, a bunch of test domains are set up in a local Kubernetes cluster.&#xA;You can use these domains to test and evaluate Uitsmijter.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;cheese-tenant-example-domains&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Cheese tenant example domains&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/test_cluster/#cheese-tenant-example-domains&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Cheese tenant example domains&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Cheese tenant example domains&#34; href=&#34;#cheese-tenant-example-domains&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h3 id=&#34;apiexamplecom&#34;&gt;&#xA;        api.example.com&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/test_cluster/#apiexamplecom&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: api.example.com&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: api.example.com&#34; href=&#34;#apiexamplecom&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This domain does not have an endpoint. This domain is used for tests and return a &lt;code&gt;404&lt;/code&gt; page not found when called.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Development guidelines</title>
      <link>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/guidelines/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/guidelines/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h1 id=&#34;development-guidelines&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Development guidelines&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/guidelines/#development-guidelines&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Development guidelines&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Development guidelines&#34; href=&#34;#development-guidelines&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;pull-requests-are-very-much-desired&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Pull requests are very much desired&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/guidelines/#pull-requests-are-very-much-desired&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Pull requests are very much desired&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Pull requests are very much desired&#34; href=&#34;#pull-requests-are-very-much-desired&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Please open a new branch with the naming scheme &lt;code&gt;feature/&amp;lt;#Issue&amp;gt;-&amp;lt;#Description&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;fix/&amp;lt;#Issue&amp;gt;-&amp;lt;#Description&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;regarding the type of the change. Do a descriptive pull request against the &lt;code&gt;main&lt;/code&gt; branch. Prepare the pull request;&#xA;we prefer small requests, that are squashed into the main branch.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Overall Goals</title>
      <link>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/goals/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/goals/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h1 id=&#34;overall-project-goals&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Overall Project Goals&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/goals/#overall-project-goals&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Overall Project Goals&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Overall Project Goals&#34; href=&#34;#overall-project-goals&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The overall project goals encompass a range of objectives that go beyond the functional requirements of the system.&#xA;These goals primarily focus on the non-functional aspects, aiming to ensure the system&amp;rsquo;s performance, reliability,&#xA;security, and usability. By considering these non-functional requirements, the project aims to deliver a robust and&#xA;user-friendly solution that meets the standards of quality and user satisfaction.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Frequently Asked Questions</title>
      <link>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/faq/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/faq/</guid>
      <description>&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h1 id=&#34;why-there-is-no-admin-interface-for-uitsmijter&#34;&gt;&#xA;        Why there is no Admin-Interface for Uitsmijter?&#xA;        &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/faq/#why-there-is-no-admin-interface-for-uitsmijter&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Why there is no Admin-Interface for Uitsmijter?&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Why there is no Admin-Interface for Uitsmijter?&#34; href=&#34;#why-there-is-no-admin-interface-for-uitsmijter&#34;&gt;&#xA;            &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Adding an admin UI to the server software can have its drawbacks and may not be the best approach for the following&#xA;reasons:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;There should be one way to do it (see &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://docs.uitsmijter.io/contribution/goals&#34;&#xA;&gt;Project Goals&lt;/a&gt;: Introducing an admin UI means providing&#xA;one other way to configure and manage the server software that is hard to sync back to descriptive files in&#xA;Kubernetes. This can limit flexibility and customization options for users who prefer different tools for editing&#xA;configuration files. By sticking solely to YAML configuration files, users&#xA;can leverage their preferred text editors, version control systems, and automation tools, allowing for greater&#xA;flexibility and compatibility with existing workflows.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;YAML configuration files provide a well-established and widely adopted method for configuring&#xA;server software. They are human-readable, versionable, and easy to share, making them a popular choice for many&#xA;server administrators. Adding an admin UI alongside configuration files may introduce confusion and complexity by&#xA;having multiple ways to configure the software, potentially leading to configuration inconsistencies and conflicts.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining an admin UI requires additional effort and resources. It involves designing and&#xA;implementing a user-friendly interface, handling user input validation, managing UI-specific issues, and keeping the&#xA;UI in sync with any changes or updates to the underlying server software. This added complexity can increase&#xA;development and maintenance overhead. This is subtracted from the time spent working on an understandable and easy to&#xA;use descriptive setting.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Server administrators are typically comfortable working with the command line and text-based interfaces. They are&#xA;accustomed to configuring and managing server software through the console and may prefer the flexibility and&#xA;efficiency it offers. Introducing an admin UI may not align with the preferences and expectations of the target&#xA;audience, potentially resulting in a less intuitive or less efficient user experience.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Web-based admin interfaces introduce additional security risks, such as potential vulnerabilities in the UI&#xA;framework, the need for proper authentication and authorization mechanisms, and the potential for cross-site&#xA;scripting (XSS) or other web-related attacks. By avoiding an admin UI, you can minimize the attack surface and reduce&#xA;the potential for security breaches associated with web-based interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;An admin UI is the entry to hiding complexity behind shiny buttons and checkboxes. We do not want to hide complexity,&#xA;we want to avid it at the first place.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This explains why Uitsmijter does not and will never have an administrative interface.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
